WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.010
A tall pendulum clock stands in a hallway,

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.410
its pendulum swinging steadily to and fro.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:11.180
Each swing takes the same time, and
the clock simply counts the swings.

4
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.150
On Earth, it keeps perfect time.

5
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.610
Now ship that same clock to the Moon.

6
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.980
Same pendulum, same clock.

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.880
Will it run fast, run slow, or keep time?

8
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:27.050
In this mission, you'll find out what
sets the period of a mass bouncing on a

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.070
spring.

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.880
Then you'll do the same for a pendulum,
and sort the changes that matter from

11
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.440
the ones that don't.

12
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:36.640
Your mission: predict
whether the clock runs fast,

13
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.470
runs slow, or keeps time on the Moon.
